  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Poverty and Inequality in Urban Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regeneration is the aim of this project. In Phnom Penh there is around 300 informal settlements where people have made their home and have a lack of water and sanitation. Although Cambodia is one of the fastest growing economies the country remains one of the most least developed. A problem we can&apos;t tackle alone, partnered with University of New South Wales we are able to access their resources to help build up resilience from the bottom, using their support for research to build a better slum</narrative>
  </description>
